INSERT INTO `wp_posts` VALUES (213,0,'2026-10-10 05:43:24','2026-10-10 05:43:24','','High Hydration Artisan Sourdough Boule','','inherit','open','closed','','high-hydration-artisan-sourdough-boule','','','2026-10-10 05:43:24','2026-10-10 05:43:24','',206,'http://localhost:8885/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/sourdough-hydration.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0);
INSERT INTO `wp_posts` VALUES (214,0,'2026-10-10 05:43:25','2026-10-10 05:43:25','\n<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"typography":{"fontSize":"1.2rem","lineHeight":"1.7"}},"textColor":"secondary-text"} -->\n<p class="has-secondary-text-color" style="font-size:1.2rem;line-height:1.7">Few ingredients command greater culinary reverence than true extra virgin olive oil. Yet beneath the romantic pastoral labels lies a complex biochemical landscape governed by mechanical shear forces, enzymatic oxidation, and temperature thresholds.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:pattern {"slug":"nourish-pure/table-of-contents"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {"level":2} -->\n<h2 id="understanding-the-science">The Science of Polyphenols &amp; Cold Extraction</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>During the traditional <em>frantoio</em> milling process, freshly harvested drupes pass through granite stones or low-speed stainless hammer mills. European and international regulatory standards mandate that olive oil labeled "cold-pressed" or "cold-extracted" must never exceed 27&deg;C (80.6&deg;F) during the malaxation phase.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>When temperatures climb beyond this crucial limit, volatile aromatics such as hexanal (responsible for fresh green apple and cut-grass notes) evaporate. More crucially, oleocanthal—the natural anti-inflammatory phenolic compound that imparts the characteristic peppery tickle in the back of the throat—degrades rapidly.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:pattern {"slug":"nourish-pure/editorial-callout"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {"level":2} -->\n<h2 id="essential-equipment">Comparing Culinary Fats &amp; Smoke Points</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>To understand where cold-pressed olive oil shines best, consider how its extraction method and fatty acid structure compare with other common culinary oils:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:pattern {"slug":"nourish-pure/comparison-table"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:pattern {"slug":"nourish-pure/caution-note"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:pattern {"slug":"nourish-pure/pull-quote"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {"level":2} -->\n<h2 id="tasting-notes">Tasting Notes &amp; Kitchen Applications</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Reserve your most robust, early-harvest monocultivar oils for raw finishing: spooned over warm cannellini beans, drizzled onto grilled sourdough rubbed with garlic, or emulsified with citrus juice for bitter chicory greens.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n		','The Living Architecture of Cold-Pressed Olive Oils: Harvest, Phenols, and Flame','Why thermal friction destroys delicate polyphenols, and how small-batch hydraulic milling preserves the true peppery signature of early autumn harvest.','inherit','closed','closed','','201-revision-v1','','','2026-10-10 05:43:25','2026-10-10 05:43:25','',201,'http://localhost:8885/?p=214',0,'revision','',0);
INSERT INTO `wp_posts` VALUES (215,0,'2026-10-10 05:43:25','2026-10-10 05:43:25','\n<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"typography":{"fontSize":"1.15rem","lineHeight":"1.7"}}} -->\n<p>When autumn winds arrive, our kitchen instinctively turns to clear, deeply flavorful broths. Unlike rich animal stocks that require 12 hours of simmering, this vegetable broth derives its foundational umami from high-temperature roasting.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>By roasting halved plum tomatoes until their edges blacken and slicing fennel bulbs into caramelized wedges, the natural sugars caramelize into deep, roasted sweetness without requiring added sugar or concentrates.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:pattern {"slug":"nourish-pure/recipe-card"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:pattern {"slug":"nourish-pure/editorial-callout"} /-->\n		','Rustic Roasted Fennel &amp; Charred Plum Tomato Broth','A deeply caramelized, comforting vegetal broth infused with crushed coriander seed, whole star anise, and slow-roasted plum tomatoes.','inherit','closed','closed','','202-revision-v1','','','2026-10-10 05:43:25','2026-10-10 05:43:25','',202,'http://localhost:8885/?p=215',0,'revision','',0);
INSERT INTO `wp_posts` VALUES (216,0,'2026-10-10 05:43:25','2026-10-10 05:43:25','\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The marketing surrounding cold-pressed juices often makes bold claims regarding live enzymes and bioavailable minerals. In our kitchen lab, we set out to rigorously test whether slow vertical mastication truly justifies its premium over traditional high-speed spinning blades.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:pattern {"slug":"nourish-pure/beverage-spotlight"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {"level":2} -->\n<h2>Key Findings From Lab Extraction</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Our infrared thermometer recorded an average temperature increase of 4.2&deg;C in centrifugal chambers running at 14,000 RPM, compared to just 0.4&deg;C in slow masticating augers running at 45 RPM. This temperature difference directly correlated with foam volume and subsequent rapid browning within 2 hours of refrigeration.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n		','Hydraulic Mastication vs Centrifugal Juicing: A Micronutrient Breakdown','We measured yield, temperature change, and oxidation rates across four juicing mechanisms to determine the true value of cold hydraulic mastication.','inherit','closed','closed','','203-revision-v1','','','2026-10-10 05:43:25','2026-10-10 05:43:25','',203,'http://localhost:8885/?p=216',0,'revision','',0);
INSERT INTO `wp_posts` VALUES (217,0,'2026-10-10 05:43:25','2026-10-10 05:43:25','\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Commercial white vinegar is largely synthesized from petroleum-derived ethanol in massive stainless steel submerged-bubble fermenters within 24 hours. In contrast, traditional vinegar makers employ the slow, surface-dwelling <em>Orleans</em> method, taking upwards of six months to craft vinegar with unparalleled aromatic complexity.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:pattern {"slug":"nourish-pure/how-its-made"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The resulting vinegar retains trace esters, higher alcohols, and pleasant volatile acids that commercial rapid production strips away.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n		','Inside Small-Batch Vinegar Production: From Raw Pomace to Acetification','An educational tour through artisanal acetification, French Orleans barrel aging, and how acetic acid bacteria transform fruit wines into complex pantry staples.','inherit','closed','closed','','204-revision-v1','','','2026-10-10 05:43:25','2026-10-10 05:43:25','',204,'http://localhost:8885/?p=217',0,'revision','',0);
INSERT INTO `wp_posts` VALUES (218,0,'2026-10-10 05:43:25','2026-10-10 05:43:25','\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In a world overflowing with thousand-dollar automated espresso stations, the humble piston-driven AeroPress continues to outshine far more complex brewing setups for light, delicate, washed single-origin coffees.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:pattern {"slug":"nourish-pure/product-review"} /-->\n		','Tested: The AeroPress Original for Specialty Light-Roast Extraction','After four months of daily testing with washed Ethiopian coffees, we analyze why this unassuming plastic cylinder remains the benchmark for low-sediment home brewing.','inherit','closed','closed','','205-revision-v1','','','2026-10-10 05:43:25','2026-10-10 05:43:25','',205,'http://localhost:8885/?p=218',0,'revision','',0);
INSERT INTO `wp_posts` VALUES (219,0,'2026-10-10 05:43:26','2026-10-10 05:43:26','\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Social media has fostered an obsession with 85%+ hydration sourdough bread, often leading novice bakers into frustrated encounters with slack, unmanageable dough pancakes. In this guide, we explore how flour protein absorption actually works.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:pattern {"slug":"nourish-pure/downloadable-guide"} /-->\n		','The Hydration Spectrum: Demystifying 65% to 85% Sourdough Doughs','Understanding baker\'s percentages, flour ash content, and why chasing ultra-high hydration often compromises crust texture and crumb gelatinization.','inherit','closed','closed','','206-revision-v1','','','2026-10-10 05:43:26','2026-10-10 05:43:26','',206,'http://localhost:8885/?p=219',0,'revision','',0);
